{
    "//" : [
        "cicpy technology rules for gf180mcuD (Ciel f6eeac7dad085ffcc829ccfd721f7b4ce39edcf7).",
        "",
        "UNITS. cicpy stores coordinates in the unit implied by its magic",
        "reader: Magic.toAngstrom() is file_units/magscale*100. gf180mcuD",
        "writes .mag files with 'magscale 1 10' and one file unit is 5 nm of",
        "silicon, so one cicpy unit is 0.5 nm, not 1 A. gamma is therefore 20,",
        "not the 100 a sky130 tech file uses, and every rule number below is",
        "plain micrometre * 100 (M1 width 0.23 um -> 23). Measured, not",
        "assumed: the gencell gate of a w=2 l=0.5 device is 100x400 file units.",
        "",
        "GRID. cicpy_gf180.patch_magic_scale() replaces MagicPrinter's sky130",
        "scale, so one written unit is one Magic internal unit -- exactly the",
        "5 nm manufacturing grid -- instead of 25 nm, which cannot express a",
        "0.26 um via1. The writer therefore quantises to the grid by",
        "construction and gridcheck, which tests cicpy's un-rounded internal",
        "coordinate rather than the number written, is off.",
        "",
        "ALIASES are magic paint-type names (gf180mcuD.tech 'types' section),",
        "because Magic.parseToken() resolves a '<< name >>' section header",
        "through Rules.aliasToLayer(). LAYER NUMBERS are the calma numbers of",
        "the magic 'cifoutput style gdsii' section.",
        "",
        "DESIGN RULES are the gf180mcuD magic drc section, converted from its",
        "nanometre values (M1.1 width 230 -> 23)."
    ],
    "version" : 2,
